From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OodavidsinoO <david.sin@tuta.io>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Skip frame decode for Dolby Vision videos

MiuiCamera's thumbnail loader tries two sources in order: the cover box that
the app itself writes into the MP4, and, when that is missing, a real frame
decode through MediaMetadataRetriever.

On this device the second path never returns for Dolby Vision files. The
Dolby Vision Codec2 decoder (c2.dolby.hevc.dec.so) self-deadlocks in
onRelease(): it posts a blocking message to the looper that is executing
onRelease(), so the reply can never be delivered. MediaCodec::release() then
waits forever inside ALooper::awaitResponse(), and because
MetadataRetrieverClient holds a process-wide lock across the whole call,
every later thumbnail or metadata request in mediaserver hangs too -- the
symptom is an ordinary recording saved as .pending-<name>.mp4.

The blob is byte-identical to the official HyperOS 3.0.306.0 build, so the
defect cannot be fixed by updating it, and it cannot be patched in place.

The framework now bounds both waits, but the cheapest fix is to not enter the
path at all: a Dolby Vision recording already carries the cover the app wrote,
and decoding is only ever the fallback. Detect the mimetype before decoding
and bail out, which lets the caller keep whatever the cover box produced.

Detected via METADATA_KEY_MIMETYPE (12); the string "dolby-vision" is what
MPEG4Extractor reports for a track carrying a dvvC box. Throwing here is
caught by the existing handler in the same method, which logs and returns
null, i.e. "no thumbnail from decode" -- exactly the desired outcome.

--- a/smali/A/a4.smali	2026-10-20 12:53:12.867768493 +0800
+++ b/smali/A/a4.smali	2026-10-20 12:53:50.624201410 +0800
@@ -1378,6 +1378,31 @@
     invoke-virtual {v0, p3, p4}, Landroid/media/MediaMetadataRetriever;->setDataSource(Landroid/content/Context;Landroid/net/Uri;)V
 
     :goto_1
+    const/16 p1, 0xc
+
+    invoke-virtual {v0, p1}, Landroid/media/MediaMetadataRetriever;->extractMetadata(I)Ljava/lang/String;
+
+    move-result-object p1
+
+    if-eqz p1, :cond_dv
+
+    const-string p2, "dolby-vision"
+
+    invoke-virtual {p1, p2}, Ljava/lang/String;->contains(Ljava/lang/CharSequence;)Z
+
+    move-result p1
+
+    if-eqz p1, :cond_dv
+
+    new-instance p1, Ljava/lang/IllegalArgumentException;
+
+    const-string p2, "skip dolby vision frame decode"
+
+    invoke-direct {p1, p2}, Ljava/lang/IllegalArgumentException;-><init>(Ljava/lang/String;)V
+
+    throw p1
+
+    :cond_dv
     const/16 p1, 0x18
 
     invoke-virtual {v0, p1}, Landroid/media/MediaMetadataRetriever;->extractMetadata(I)Ljava/lang/String;
